**Status**: Approved
**Author**: NMG
**Related Spec**: specs/503-fix-duplicate-changelog-entry-when-delivery-rolls-a-hand-written-issue-entry/

# File: scripts/__tests__/sdlc-deliver.test.mjs
# Generated from: specs/512-file-generated-bug-fix-changelog-lines-under-fixed/requirements.md
Feature: Generated CHANGELOG lines use the issue's category

  @SCN001 @regression
  Scenario: A bug issue's generated line is filed under Fixed
    Given issue #42 titled "Deliver verified changes" is labelled "bug" with no BREAKING declaration
    And CHANGELOG.md has an empty [Unreleased] section
    When prepare-version runs for issue #42
    Then the new release section contains "### Fixed" followed by "- Deliver verified changes (#42)"
    And the new release section contains no "### Changed" heading

  @SCN002 @regression
  Scenario: The generated line joins an existing Fixed section
    Given issue #42 is labelled "bug"
    And [Unreleased] contains "### Fixed" with "- Corrected the widget (#7)" followed by "### Changed" with "- Renamed the option (#8)"
    When prepare-version runs for issue #42
    Then the new release section contains exactly one "### Fixed" heading
    And "- Deliver verified changes (#42)" directly follows "- Corrected the widget (#7)"
    And "### Changed" with "- Renamed the option (#8)" follows in its original form

  @SCN003 @regression
  Scenario: A feature issue's generated line stays under Changed
    Given issue #42 is labelled "enhancement" with no BREAKING declaration
    And [Unreleased] contains "### Changed" with "- Renamed the option (#8)"
    When prepare-version runs for issue #42
    Then the new release section contains exactly one "### Changed" heading ending with "- Deliver verified changes (#42)"
    And the new release section contains no "### Fixed" heading

  @SCN004 @regression
  Scenario: An approved breaking bug fix stays under Changed (BREAKING)
    Given issue #42 is labelled "bug" and titled "BREAKING: Deliver verified changes"
    And the approved requirements contain "**Version bump**: major"
    When prepare-version runs for issue #42
    Then VERSION is bumped to the next major
    And "- BREAKING: Deliver verified changes (#42)" is filed under "### Changed (BREAKING)"
    And no "### Fixed" heading is added

  @SCN005 @regression
  Scenario: Re-running preparation for a bug issue does not bump again
    Given prepare-version already filed issue #42's generated line under "### Fixed" and committed the version artifacts
    When prepare-version runs again for issue #42
    Then it reports the same prepared version
    And VERSION, package.json, and CHANGELOG.md are unchanged and no new commit is created
